  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duns">Duns</ref> 8.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et qui aduocat, unus et solus iuret, quod ad manum illam uocet, que uendidit ei.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ se ðe hit tyme, sylle ana ðone að, þæt he hit to ðære handa tyme, þe him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-b">And he who guarantees it [the security sworn to] must swear alone the oath: that he warrants that sold the cattle to the person (accuser).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wer es zur Gewähr schiebt, leiste für sich allein folgenden Eid: ‘dass er es zu dér Hand schiebe, die [es] ihm veräussert hat’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let whoever vouches it to warranty give the following oath alone: ‘that he vouches it to the hand which sold [it] to him’.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="379"><ref target="clause:Swer_3-1">Swer 3.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 3, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Swer 3.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
